QR = \sqrt{PQ^2 + PR^2} = \sqrt{20^2 + 8^2} = \sqrt{400 + 64} = \sqrt{464} = \sqrt{16 \cdot 29} = 4\sqrt{29}
\] So the perimeter of $\triangle PQR$ is the sum of the sides: \[
PQ + QR + PR = 20 + 4\sqrt{29} + 8 = 28 + 4\sqrt{29}
\] The answer is $28 + 4\sqrt{29}$. </think> <answer> 28+4*sqrt(29) </answer>

